1
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Hale County This Morning, This Evening is a
documentary film directed by RaMell Ross.

2
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Composed of intimate and unencumbered moments of people in a community, this film is constructed in a form that allows the viewer an emotive impression of the
Historic South - trumpeting the beauty of life and consequences of the social construction of race, while simultaneously a testament to dreaming.

3
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Hale County This Morning, This Evening is a 2018 American documentary film
about the lives of African Americans in Hale County, Alabama.

4
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
It is directed by RaMell Ross and produced by RaMell Ross, Joslyn
Barnes, Su Kim, and is Ross's first nonfiction feature.

5
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
The documentary is the winner of 2018 Sundance Film Festival award for U.S.

6
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
Documentary Special Jury Award for Creative Vision, 2018 Gotham Independent Film Award for Best Documentary
Feature and the Cinema Eye Honors Outstanding Achievement in Nonfiction Feature Filmmaking.

7
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:18,000
It was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature.

8
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:54,000
It was released in theaters on September 14, 2018, later aired on television as part of
the PBS series Independent Lens, and eventually won a 2020 Peabody Award.

9
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:30,000
The film explores themes of alabama, family's daily life, slice
of life, american southwest, african american.
